From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0750: present_stats: what the display really showed (DXGI frame statistics, judged against the cadence), a '[present-stats]' line

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (stutter investigation on a new machine, 2026-11-27)
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: The game's frame-time counters ([mcla-sim] frame times) measure the game thread; nothing measured what reached the
  screen. Runs 2 and 3 on an RTX 4060 laptop had a flawless game thread (p99 19 ms, no missed frame) while every swap was
  late against the free-running guest vblank (vsync=false), and the log could not say whether frames were repeated or
  dropped on the panel. After every Present of the D3D12 presenter, IDXGISwapChain::GetFrameStatistics (and
  GetLastPresentCount) is sampled. What the counters really are, measured on a 165 Hz panel driven by the GPU itself
  (flip model, windowed/composed and borderless, 60 and 300 presents a second, PresentMon 2.6 as the reference):
  PresentCount counts presents RETIRED by the compositor (a present replaced before its refresh counts too) and lags
  GetLastPresentCount by 1 or 2; while the window is hidden, covered or minimised it, SyncRefreshCount and SyncQPCTime
  stop, the lag grows by one a Present, and when the window is back the whole backlog is retired in one step (a window can
  'show' more frames than it presented, or none); SyncRefreshCount/SyncQPCTime are the compositor's refresh clock, which
  with tearing allowed (variable refresh) ran at 120 to 160 Hz, never the panel's 165; PresentRefreshCount is the refresh
  at which the latest retired present is shown (a step of 0 = two presents on one refresh, the earlier never shown); the first calls
  after a swap chain is made are DISJOINT or zero; DwmGetCompositionTimingInfo is no fallback (cRefresh/cFrame count this
  process's presents, cFramesDropped stays 0).
  Judder is measured against the CADENCE, the refreshes one frame is expected to last = measured refresh rate / present rate
  (60 fps on 165 Hz = 2.75: a frame stays 2 or 3 refreshes, in a 3-3-3-2 beat, by design). A frame held longer than
  ceil(cadence) is held longer than the cadence allows; present_stats_hitch_refreshes (2) is how many refreshes beyond that
  a frame must stay for its own '[present-stats] hitch' line (at most 8 a window, judged against the cadence of the last
  2 s that were judgeable: none in the first 2 s or while the display is not taking presents). Every present_stats_log_s
  (10, 0 = off) one line:
    [present-stats] 10.0 s: presents P shown S dropped D | refreshes R at H Hz | shown frames held 1 refresh a, 2 b,
    3+ c (max m), repeats >= r | present call max x ms, over 2 ms k | present interval max y ms, over 1.5 / 2.5
    refreshes i / j | stats n ok f failed | cadence 2.75 refreshes a frame (60.0 presents/s on a 165.001 Hz refresh
    clock; display mode 165 Hz), held over 3 refreshes o, hitches (>= 5 refreshes) h, present interval over 1.5 / 2.5
    times the mean u / v | reliable
  where S = frames that had a refresh of their own (sum of min(retired, refreshes advanced)), D = presents replaced before
  they were shown (S + D ~ presents), the held counts are absolute (as before: 1, 2, 3+ refreshes) and 'repeats >= r' is the
  sum of the refreshes beyond ceil(cadence). A window whose display statistics cannot be trusted - a GetFrameStatistics
  failure or restart (DISJOINT after the first), a counter jump, more than 8 presents in flight (the window hidden, covered
  or minimised), the refresh clock covering under 90% or over 110% of the window - prints '?' for every display-side number
  and ends ' | UNRELIABLE (<reason>)' instead of ' | reliable'; the CPU-side numbers (presents, present call, present
  interval) stay. A GetFrameStatistics failure other than DISJOINT is logged once with its HRESULT. Two QPC reads, one
  GetLastPresentCount and one GetFrameStatistics a present; no behaviour change.
Bucket: REDO
---
diff --git a/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp b/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
index de44d87..d11ae21 100644
--- a/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
+++ b/src/ui/d3d12/d3d12_presenter.cpp
@@ -13,7 +13,10 @@
 #include <climits>
 #include <cmath>
 #include <memory>
+#include <mutex>   // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0750)
+#include <string>  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0750)
 #include <utility>
+#include <vector>  // LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0750)
 
 #include <rex/assert.h>
 #include <rex/cvar.h>
@@ -33,9 +36,412 @@
 
 REXCVAR_DEFINE_BOOL(d3d12_allow_variable_refresh_rate_and_tearing, true, "UI/D3D12",
                     "Allow variable refresh rate and tearing");
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0750): what the display really showed, from DXGI's frame statistics.
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(present_stats_log_s, 10, "UI/D3D12",
+                     "Seconds between the '[present-stats]' lines (0 = off): presents made, frames the display "
+                     "showed, frames dropped (replaced before they were shown), how many refreshes each shown frame "
+                     "stayed on screen against the cadence (the refresh rate over the present rate: 1 at 60 fps on "
+                     "60 Hz, 2.75 at 60 fps on 165 Hz, where 2 and 3 are normal), the measured refresh rate, and how "
+                     "long the Present call itself took. A window in which the display's statistics cannot be "
+                     "trusted (the window hidden or covered, a mode change) is marked UNRELIABLE, with the reason, "
+                     "instead of counts. The frame-time counters of the game measure the game thread; these are what "
+                     "reached the screen")
+    .range(0, 3600)
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(present_stats_hitch_refreshes, 2, "UI/D3D12",
+                     "A shown frame that stayed this many refreshes longer on screen than the cadence allows (the "
+                     "cadence rounded up: 3 at 60 fps on 165 Hz, 1 at 60 fps on 60 Hz) gets its own "
+                     "'[present-stats] hitch' line (at most 8 a log window), to match against '[mcla-hitch]'. "
+                     "0 = none")
+    .range(0, 1000)
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
 
 namespace rex::ui::d3d12 {
 
+// LOCAL PATCH - MCLA (0750) begin: present statistics. Fed once per Present on the paint path (the UI thread or the
+// guest output thread, never both at once; the mutex keeps it safe anyway).
+//
+// What IDXGISwapChain::GetFrameStatistics really reports (measured on a 165 Hz panel driven by an RTX 4060 laptop
+// GPU, flip-model swap chain, windowed (composed by the DWM) and borderless, with PresentMon 2.6 as the reference):
+//  * PresentCount is the number of presents the compositor has RETIRED, not the number shown: a present replaced
+//    before its refresh counts too. It lags GetLastPresentCount by one or two presents. While the window is hidden,
+//    covered or minimised it stops (the lag then grows by one on every Present) and, when the window is visible again,
+//    the whole backlog is retired in one step: a log window can "show" more frames than it presented, or none.
+//  * SyncRefreshCount / SyncQPCTime are the refresh clock of the compositor. They stop and jump with it, and are not
+//    the panel's own: with tearing allowed (variable refresh) the clock ran at 120 to 160 Hz on this 165 Hz panel.
+//  * PresentRefreshCount is the refresh at which the latest retired present is shown. Between two samples one retired
+//    present with dPresentRefreshCount = n means that the frame before it stayed n refreshes on screen; n = 0 means
+//    two presents landed on one refresh, the earlier was never shown (content faster than the refresh).
+//  * The first calls after a swap chain is made fail with DXGI_ERROR_FRAME_STATISTICS_DISJOINT or return zeros.
+//  * DwmGetCompositionTimingInfo is no fallback: its cRefresh / cFrame count this process's presents (one a Present),
+//    cFrameDisplayed stays 0 and cFramesDropped / Late / Missed stay 0 even at 300 presents a second on 165 Hz.
+// A window of the log is therefore judged only when all of these hold: the calls succeeded and the counters were
+// continuous, at most kPresentStatsMaxInFlight presents were ever in flight (made, not yet retired), and the refresh
+// clock covered the window (0.9 to 1.1 of its time). Otherwise the display-side numbers are printed as '?', with the
+// reason. Judged frames are compared with the cadence, the refreshes a frame is expected to last: the refresh rate
+// over the present rate (1 at 60 fps on 60 Hz; 2.75 at 60 fps on 165 Hz, where 2 and 3 are normal, in a 3-3-3-2 beat).
+namespace {
+
+constexpr int32_t kPresentStatsMaxInFlight = 8;
+constexpr size_t kPresentStatsMaxIntervals = 1 << 16;
+constexpr uint32_t kPresentStatsHeldBins = 32;  // refreshes a frame stayed: 0 to 30, the last bin is 31 or more
+constexpr double kPresentStatsSliceS = 2.0;      // the cadence the hitch lines are judged against: of the last 2 s
+
+class PresentStats {
+ public:
+  void OnPresent(IDXGISwapChain* swap_chain, HRESULT result, int64_t start_qpc, int64_t end_qpc) {
+    const int32_t log_s = REXCVAR_GET(present_stats_log_s);
+    if (log_s <= 0 || !swap_chain) {
+      return;
+    }
+    std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex_);
+    if (!qpf_) {
+      LARGE_INTEGER f;
+      QueryPerformanceFrequency(&f);
+      qpf_ = f.QuadPart > 0 ? f.QuadPart : 1;
+    }
+    if (window_start_qpc_ == 0) {
+      window_start_qpc_ = start_qpc;
+    }
+    ++w_.presents;
+    if (FAILED(result)) {
+      ++w_.failed;
+    }
+    const double call_ms = double(end_qpc - start_qpc) * 1000.0 / double(qpf_);
+    w_.call_max_ms = std::max(w_.call_max_ms, call_ms);
+    if (call_ms > 2.0) {
+      ++w_.call_over_2ms;
+    }
+    if (last_present_qpc_ != 0) {
+      const double interval_ms = double(start_qpc - last_present_qpc_) * 1000.0 / double(qpf_);
+      w_.interval_max_ms = std::max(w_.interval_max_ms, interval_ms);
+      if (intervals_ms_.size() < kPresentStatsMaxIntervals) {
+        intervals_ms_.push_back(float(interval_ms));
+      }
+    }
+    last_present_qpc_ = start_qpc;
+    if (slice_.start_qpc == 0) {
+      slice_.start_qpc = start_qpc;
+    }
+    ++slice_.presents;
+
+    UINT last_count = 0;
+    const bool have_last = SUCCEEDED(swap_chain->GetLastPresentCount(&last_count));
+    DXGI_FRAME_STATISTICS st{};
+    const HRESULT sr = swap_chain->GetFrameStatistics(&st);
+    if (SUCCEEDED(sr)) {
+      ++w_.stats_ok;
+      if (st.SyncRefreshCount == 0 && st.SyncQPCTime.QuadPart == 0) {
+        // Not valid yet: the first calls after the swap chain was made return zeros.
+        have_prev_ = false;
+      } else {
+        have_valid_ = true;
+        OnStatistics(st, have_last ? int32_t(last_count - st.PresentCount) : 0);
+      }
+    } else {
+      ++w_.stats_failed;
+      if (sr == DXGI_ERROR_FRAME_STATISTICS_DISJOINT) {
+        // The first call after the swap chain is made is always disjoint; a later one is a display or mode change.
+        if (have_valid_) {
+          ++w_.disjoint;
+        }
+      } else {
+        ++w_.stats_failed_other;
+        w_.last_failure = sr;
+        if (!warned_stats_) {
+          warned_stats_ = true;
+          REXLOG_WARN("[present-stats] GetFrameStatistics failed (HRESULT 0x{:08X}): only the CPU side of the "
+                      "presents is counted",
+                      uint32_t(sr));
+        }
+      }
+      have_prev_ = false;
+      slice_.broken = true;
+    }
+    AdvanceSlice(end_qpc);
+
+    const double window_s = double(end_qpc - window_start_qpc_) / double(qpf_);
+    if (window_s < double(log_s)) {
+      return;
+    }
+    LogWindow(swap_chain, window_s);
+    w_ = Window{};
+    intervals_ms_.clear();
+    window_start_qpc_ = end_qpc;
+  }
+
+ private:
+  // The refreshes one shown frame is expected to last: the refresh rate over the present rate. `allowed` is that
+  // rounded up (with a little tolerance for the two rates being measured apart): a frame held longer than that was
+  // held longer than the cadence allows.
+  struct Cadence {
+    double refresh_ms = 0.0, hz = 0.0, present_rate = 0.0, value = 0.0;
+    int32_t allowed = 0;
+  };
+
+  // The last stretch (kPresentStatsSliceS) of presents and refresh clock, for the cadence the hitch lines are judged
+  // against: it follows the content (a loading screen at 100 presents a second, then the drive at 60) within seconds,
+  // where the cadence of a whole log window averages them.
+  struct Slice {
+    int64_t start_qpc = 0;
+    uint64_t presents = 0, sync_refreshes = 0;
+    int64_t sync_qpc = 0;
+    int32_t in_flight_max = 0;
+    bool broken = false;  // a failed call or a counter jump inside it
+  };
+
+  struct Window {
+    uint64_t presents = 0, failed = 0;
+    uint64_t retired = 0, shown = 0, dropped = 0, sync_refreshes = 0;
+    int64_t sync_qpc = 0;
+    uint64_t held_hist[kPresentStatsHeldBins] = {};
+    uint32_t held_max = 0;
+    uint64_t multi_frames = 0, multi_refreshes = 0;
+    double call_max_ms = 0.0;
+    uint64_t call_over_2ms = 0;
+    double interval_max_ms = 0.0;
+    int32_t in_flight_max = 0;
+    uint64_t stats_ok = 0, stats_failed = 0, stats_failed_other = 0, disjoint = 0, resets = 0;
+    HRESULT last_failure = S_OK;
+    uint32_t hitch_lines = 0;
+    uint64_t hitch_unlogged = 0;
+  };
+
+  Cadence MakeCadence(uint64_t presents, double window_s, uint64_t sync_refreshes, int64_t sync_qpc) const {
+    Cadence c;
+    if (sync_refreshes > 0 && sync_qpc > 0) {
+      c.refresh_ms = double(sync_qpc) * 1000.0 / double(qpf_) / double(sync_refreshes);
+      c.hz = 1000.0 / c.refresh_ms;
+    }
+    if (window_s > 0.0 && presents > 1) {
+      c.present_rate = double(presents) / window_s;
+    }
+    if (c.hz > 0.0 && c.present_rate > 0.0) {
+      c.value = c.hz / c.present_rate;
+      c.allowed = std::max(1, int32_t(std::ceil(c.value - 0.08)));
+    }
+    return c;
+  }
+
+  void AdvanceSlice(int64_t now_qpc) {
+    const double secs = double(now_qpc - slice_.start_qpc) / double(qpf_);
+    if (slice_.start_qpc == 0 || secs < kPresentStatsSliceS) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const double coverage = double(slice_.sync_qpc) / double(qpf_) / secs;
+    recent_ = Cadence{};
+    if (!slice_.broken && slice_.in_flight_max <= kPresentStatsMaxInFlight && coverage >= 0.9 && coverage <= 1.1) {
+      recent_ = MakeCadence(slice_.presents, secs, slice_.sync_refreshes, slice_.sync_qpc);
+    }
+    slice_ = Slice{};
+    slice_.start_qpc = now_qpc;
+  }
+
+  // Fed with every valid sample. in_flight = presents made but not yet retired by the compositor.
+  void OnStatistics(const DXGI_FRAME_STATISTICS& st, int32_t in_flight) {
+    w_.in_flight_max = std::max(w_.in_flight_max, in_flight);
+    slice_.in_flight_max = std::max(slice_.in_flight_max, in_flight);
+    if (have_prev_) {
+      const uint32_t dp = st.PresentCount - prev_.PresentCount;
+      const uint32_t dr = st.PresentRefreshCount - prev_.PresentRefreshCount;
+      const uint32_t ds = st.SyncRefreshCount - prev_.SyncRefreshCount;
+      // Sanity: a counter reset (mode change, swap chain recreated) shows as a huge or backwards step.
+      if (dp < 100000 && dr < 100000 && ds < 100000) {
+        w_.retired += dp;
+        // Of dp presents retired in this step, at most dr can have had a refresh of their own.
+        w_.shown += std::min(dp, dr);
+        w_.dropped += dp > dr ? dp - dr : 0;
+        w_.sync_refreshes += ds;
+        slice_.sync_refreshes += ds;
+        if (ds > 0) {
+          w_.sync_qpc += st.SyncQPCTime.QuadPart - prev_.SyncQPCTime.QuadPart;
+          slice_.sync_qpc += st.SyncQPCTime.QuadPart - prev_.SyncQPCTime.QuadPart;
+        }
+        if (dp == 1 && dr > 0 && in_flight <= kPresentStatsMaxInFlight) {
+          // The frame before the newly shown one stayed dr refreshes.
+          ++w_.held_hist[std::min(dr, kPresentStatsHeldBins - 1)];
+          w_.held_max = std::max(w_.held_max, dr);
+          OnHeld(dr);
+        } else if (dp > 1) {
+          // Sampled less often than frames were retired: dr refreshes for dp frames, not attributable one by one.
+          w_.multi_frames += dp;
+          w_.multi_refreshes += dr;
+        }
+      } else {
+        ++w_.resets;
+        slice_.broken = true;
+      }
+    }
+    prev_ = st;
+    have_prev_ = true;
+  }
+
+  // A hitch line the moment it is seen (to match against '[mcla-hitch]'), judged against the cadence of the last
+  // 2 s that were judgeable (none in the first 2 s, or while the display is not taking presents: no line then).
+  void OnHeld(uint32_t dr) {
+    const int32_t extra = REXCVAR_GET(present_stats_hitch_refreshes);
+    if (extra <= 0) {
+      return;
+    }
+    const Cadence& c = recent_;
+    if (c.allowed <= 0 || dr < uint32_t(c.allowed + extra)) {
+      return;
+    }
+    if (w_.hitch_lines < 8) {
+      ++w_.hitch_lines;
+      REXLOG_INFO(
+          "[present-stats] hitch: a frame stayed {} refreshes on screen ({:.1f} ms) before the next (cadence {:.2f} "
+          "refreshes a frame: up to {} is normal)",
+          dr, dr * c.refresh_ms, c.value, c.allowed);
+    } else {
+      ++w_.hitch_unlogged;
+    }
+  }
+
+  // Why the display-side numbers of this window cannot be trusted, or an empty string when they can.
+  std::string UnreliableReason(double window_s) const {
+    if (w_.stats_ok == 0) {
+      return fmt::format("GetFrameStatistics never succeeded ({} calls failed)", w_.stats_failed);
+    }
+    if (w_.stats_failed_other) {
+      return fmt::format("GetFrameStatistics failed {} times (HRESULT 0x{:08X})", w_.stats_failed_other,
+                         uint32_t(w_.last_failure));
+    }
+    if (w_.disjoint) {
+      return fmt::format("the display statistics restarted {} times (a display, mode or window change)", w_.disjoint);
+    }
+    if (w_.resets) {
+      return fmt::format("the counters jumped {} times", w_.resets);
+    }
+    if (w_.in_flight_max > kPresentStatsMaxInFlight) {
+      return fmt::format(
+          "the display stopped taking presents for part of the window ({} presents queued, {} of {} retired): the "
+          "window was hidden, covered or minimised, or the display was off",
+          w_.in_flight_max, w_.retired, w_.presents);
+    }
+    if (w_.presents < 2 || w_.sync_refreshes == 0 || w_.sync_qpc <= 0) {
+      return fmt::format("too few presents or refreshes to judge ({} presents, {} refreshes)", w_.presents,
+                         w_.sync_refreshes);
+    }
+    const double coverage = double(w_.sync_qpc) / double(qpf_) / window_s;
+    if (coverage < 0.9 || coverage > 1.1) {
+      return fmt::format("the refresh counter covered {:.0f}% of the window's time", coverage * 100.0);
+    }
+    return std::string();
+  }
+
+  // The refresh rate of the monitor the swap chain is shown on, as set in Windows (0 if unknown).
+  static double DisplayModeHz(IDXGISwapChain* swap_chain) {
+    Microsoft::WRL::ComPtr<IDXGIOutput> output;
+    DXGI_OUTPUT_DESC desc{};
+    DEVMODEW mode{};
+    mode.dmSize = sizeof(mode);
+    if (FAILED(swap_chain->GetContainingOutput(&output)) || FAILED(output->GetDesc(&desc)) ||
+        !EnumDisplaySettingsW(desc.DeviceName, ENUM_CURRENT_SETTINGS, &mode)) {
+      return 0.0;
+    }
+    return mode.dmDisplayFrequency > 1 ? double(mode.dmDisplayFrequency) : 0.0;
+  }
+
+  void LogWindow(IDXGISwapChain* swap_chain, double window_s) {
+    const Cadence c = MakeCadence(w_.presents, window_s, w_.sync_refreshes, w_.sync_qpc);
+    const std::string why = UnreliableReason(window_s);
+    const bool ok = why.empty() && c.allowed > 0;
+    const std::string reason = why.empty() && !ok ? std::string("no cadence") : why;
+    const int32_t extra = REXCVAR_GET(present_stats_hitch_refreshes);
+    // The shown frames, by how long they stayed, against the cadence.
+    uint64_t held_3plus = 0, held_over = 0, repeats = 0, hitches = 0;
+    for (uint32_t v = 3; v < kPresentStatsHeldBins; ++v) {
+      held_3plus += w_.held_hist[v];
+    }
+    if (ok) {
+      for (uint32_t v = uint32_t(c.allowed) + 1; v < kPresentStatsHeldBins; ++v) {
+        held_over += w_.held_hist[v];
+        repeats += uint64_t(v - uint32_t(c.allowed)) * w_.held_hist[v];
+      }
+      for (uint32_t v = uint32_t(c.allowed + std::max(extra, 1)); extra > 0 && v < kPresentStatsHeldBins; ++v) {
+        hitches += w_.held_hist[v];
+      }
+    }
+    // The present intervals (the game's side), against the refresh and against their own mean.
+    uint64_t over_1_5 = 0, over_2_5 = 0, mean_over_1_5 = 0, mean_over_2_5 = 0;
+    double mean_ms = 0.0;
+    for (float v : intervals_ms_) {
+      mean_ms += v;
+    }
+    mean_ms = intervals_ms_.empty() ? 0.0 : mean_ms / double(intervals_ms_.size());
+    for (float v : intervals_ms_) {
+      if (ok && v > 1.5 * c.refresh_ms) ++over_1_5;
+      if (ok && v > 2.5 * c.refresh_ms) ++over_2_5;
+      if (mean_ms > 0.0 && v > 1.5 * mean_ms) ++mean_over_1_5;
+      if (mean_ms > 0.0 && v > 2.5 * mean_ms) ++mean_over_2_5;
+    }
+
+    const auto num = [&](uint64_t v) { return ok ? std::to_string(v) : std::string("?"); };
+    std::string tail;
+    if (ok) {
+      const double mode_hz = DisplayModeHz(swap_chain);
+      const std::string mode =
+          mode_hz > 0.0
+              ? fmt::format("; display mode {:.0f} Hz{}", mode_hz,
+                            std::fabs(c.hz - mode_hz) > 0.005 * mode_hz
+                                ? ", the clock differs from it, as with variable refresh: frames are shown when presented "
+                                  "and the held counts jitter by a tick of that clock"
+                                : "")
+              : std::string();
+      tail = fmt::format(
+          " | cadence {:.2f} refreshes a frame ({:.1f} presents/s on a {:.3f} Hz refresh clock{}), held over {} "
+          "refreshes {}{}, present interval over 1.5 / 2.5 times the mean {} / {} | reliable",
+          c.value, c.present_rate, c.hz, mode, c.allowed, held_over,
+          extra > 0 ? fmt::format(", hitches (>= {} refreshes) {}", c.allowed + extra, hitches) : std::string(),
+          mean_over_1_5, mean_over_2_5);
+    } else {
+      tail = fmt::format(
+          " | cadence ?, held over ? refreshes ?, present interval over 1.5 / 2.5 times the mean {} / {} | "
+          "UNRELIABLE ({})",
+          mean_over_1_5, mean_over_2_5, reason);
+    }
+    REXLOG_INFO(
+        "[present-stats] {:.1f} s: presents {} shown {} dropped {} | refreshes {} at {} Hz | shown frames held 1 "
+        "refresh {}, 2 {}, 3+ {} (max {}), repeats >= {}{} | present call max {:.2f} ms, over 2 ms {} | present "
+        "interval max {:.1f} ms, over 1.5 / 2.5 refreshes {} / {} | stats {} ok {} failed{}{}{}{}",
+        window_s, w_.presents, num(w_.shown), num(w_.dropped), num(w_.sync_refreshes),
+        ok ? fmt::format("{:.3f}", c.hz) : std::string("?"), num(w_.held_hist[1]), num(w_.held_hist[2]),
+        num(held_3plus), num(w_.held_max), num(repeats),
+        ok && w_.multi_frames ? fmt::format(" (+{} frames over {} refreshes sampled together)", w_.multi_frames,
+                                            w_.multi_refreshes)
+                              : std::string(),
